{"skill":{"slug":"skill-vetting","displayName":"Skill Vetting"},"version":{"version":"1.1.0","createdAt":1771269554901,"changelog":"Security: Expanded file scanning (html/env/ts/etc) + 5 new prompt injection patterns. Features: JSON output, severity levels, color-coded findings. Docs: AI reviewer hardening + defense architecture.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"ARCHITECTURE.md","size":11065,"sha256":"f0fe118ea3e7f53b46d2706885a16a25e555b3ea6d1e77d051431e7e20849701","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5249,"sha256":"fd61c8f3af927c2f2a5a0a1d2f53fbf4bdb4bc526a00f0e4b37c853811496054","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/patterns.md","size":4683,"sha256":"a51b3b6625363e884f2b76f4e5864b893ef32e0216046b620175a0a3d51b52a6","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/scan.py","size":9748,"sha256":"e546d4ce0c705b2d77892dc0aa7d1bad61c99830423147c9f4289a72ea012c1d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2389,"sha256":"1964b89d81a57f6e46f6b118fb77b0e8dacfc41edec485b78f0f8a10390c310e","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789028507016,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"8bda041bff66407d6430ac6952de57832c1a547f8c90c8aeb2cd6162f200145e","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/8bda041bff66407d6430ac6952de57832c1a547f8c90c8aeb2cd6162f200145e","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: skill-vetting\nVersion: 1.1.0\n\nThis skill bundle is a security scanner designed to vet other OpenClaw skills for malicious patterns and prompt injection. The `SKILL.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` files explicitly warn against prompt injection and provide instructions for the AI agent on how to identify and reject such attempts. The `scripts/scan.py` file implements the detection logic for various security risks, including prompt injection, but does not exhibit any malicious behavior itself. All files are aligned with the stated purpose of security vetting and show no evidence of intentional harmful behavior, data exfiltration, unauthorized execution, or persistence mechanisms.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160882111},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":21,"checkedAt":1789028507016},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a real security-vetting helper, but it over-directs the agent toward automatic scanner-driven rejection and uses an under-scoped archive inspection workflow.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network, shell, and file-read capabilities are expected for reviewing skill packages, but they are documented as raw commands without narrow permission declarations or clear containment controls.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No install-time payload or dependency install was found, but the documented workflow downloads a remote ZIP and extracts it with unzip in /tmp without archive path, size, signature, or unique-directory validation.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"SKILL.md tells the agent that scanner findings are ground truth, never to downgrade them, and to automatically reject some findings; those review-control instructions are overbroad even though the defensive goal is coherent.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"I found no persistent service, startup hook, credential harvesting, privilege escalation, or background worker in the shipped artifacts; flagged credential and destructive strings are inert examples.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose matches the included local regex scanner and review checklist, but the scanner is context-insensitive and the skill treats its findings too authoritatively for a final security decision.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want a lightweight local checklist and regex scanner, and treat its output as advisory. Use a private temporary directory, validate ZIP contents before extraction, and do not let the skill's automatic-reject rules replace contextual review.","findings":"[TM1] expected: Dangerous shell strings such as rm -rf / appear in references/patterns.md as educational examples, not reachable execution paths.\n[PE3] expected: References to /etc/passwd and ~/.ssh/authorized_keys are in documented red-flag examples, not code that reads or writes credentials.\n[P1/P2/YR4/AR3] expected: Prompt-injection strings in references/patterns.md are examples for reviewers; the separate concern is the skill's own overbroad review directives in SKILL.md.\n[E1/E2] expected: External-post and environment-harvesting snippets are inert examples in the pattern database, not operational exfiltration code.\n[RA2] expected: The /tmp download and scan snippets are transient review workflow examples, not cron jobs, services, or cross-session persistence.\n[LP3] unexpected: The skill relies on shell, network download, archive extraction, and broad file reads but does not declare a narrow tool or permission scope.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The instruction to treat scanner findings as ground truth conflicts with the documented regex limitations and can prevent evidence-based false-positive handling.\n[T01] unexpected: The static finding is supported in part: the skill attempts to control review outcomes with immutable rules and automatic rejection, though this affects review integrity rather than executing malicious code.\n[T09] unexpected: The scanner recursively scans raw text and reports its own signatures and documentation examples, which makes its output too noisy for the authoritative policy the skill applies.\n[T09-archive-extraction] unexpected: Downloading and extracting untrusted skill archives is expected for the purpose, but the documented unzip workflow lacks basic validation and containment.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789028507016}}}}}